      "message": "Caching parsed expression ASTs is a great idea to avoid redundant query parsing.\n\nTwo subtle questions on lifecycle and concurrency to verify:\n1. **Thread-safety / Statelessness of Predicates**: When `changeData.evaluatePredicateTree(predicate)` is called, does any predicate in the returned tree (or any custom plugin predicate) maintain mutable state during evaluation? Because the same cached `Predicate\u003cChangeData\u003e` instance will now be evaluated concurrently by multiple threads across different requests, all predicate nodes in the tree must be strictly stateless and thread-safe.\n2. **Project / User Context Isolation**: Is `SubmitRequirementChangeQueryBuilder.parse(expressionString)` completely pure and agnostic of project/caller context? If any predicate resolves project-scoped rules at parse time rather than at `match(ChangeData)` evaluation time, caching by `SubmitRequirementExpression` string alone could potentially cross project boundaries.",
